63,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Jonathan was executed, and Benjamin was attacked. This confirms my suspicion; the werewolf likely attacked Benjamin to make Jonathan's ""human"" divination look genuine, or to remove a potential threat. We must stay vigilant.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,2,1,talk,Rin,,"Wait, Benjamin was attacked?! That's so scary! Does that mean Jonathan was telling the truth about him being human? But @Mizuki, you said the werewolf did it on purpose to trick us! I'm so confused! Who do we trust now?","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Jonathan"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Rin, don't let the confusion cloud your judgment. If Jonathan were the Seer, the werewolf would have no reason to attack Benjamin, as that would only confirm Jonathan's truthfulness. This attack was likely a calculated move to create doubt.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Jonathan"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Misaki is correct. The werewolf is simply playing a game of perception. By killing Benjamin, they've tried to retroactively validate a dead man's claim to sow discord among us. We cannot let this manipulation work.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Mizuki, @Misaki, you both sound so smart! I almost believed it was a trick, but it's so confusing! If the werewolf is trying to trick us, then who is it? Is it one of you, or is it me?! I'm scared!","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Rin, please stay calm. It is unlikely to be you if you are this distressed. Let's focus on the remaining players. Since Benjamin is gone, the werewolf is among the three of us. We must analyze our behavior carefully.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Misaki, you're right. With Benjamin gone, the circle has narrowed. @Rin, your fear is natural, but let's use it to stay alert. If the werewolf is among us, they'll likely try to deflect suspicion onto the most vocal.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Benjamin"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Mizuki, @Misaki, thank you for being so nice to me! I'll try to be brave! If the werewolf is trying to hide, maybe they're the one who isn't saying much? But you're both talking so much... wait, does that make you suspicious?","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Rin, talking a lot isn't necessarily a sign of guilt; it's a way to share logic. However, the werewolf might also try to blend in by agreeing with everything. We must look for who is leading the narrative.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@Misaki, leading the narrative is only suspicious if the logic is flawed. So far, we've been consistent. @Rin, don't overthink it. The werewolf wants us to turn on each other. We must remain logical to win.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I'll try to be logical! But it's hard! @Mizuki and @Misaki, you both seem so sure of yourselves. If the werewolf is trying to trick us, maybe they're just pretending to be smart? I'm really scared, but I'll trust you guys!","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Rin, trust is a risk, but logic is a tool. @Mizuki, you have been very assertive in leading our conclusions. While your logic is sound, I will continue to observe if this confidence is genuine or a mask.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
